{# ============================================================
   BONFIRE VS MASTODON: the delta, and the honest reverse.

   Structure and every class string are lifted from features.njk;
   nothing new is invented here. Edit the `sections` array below,
   the markup loops over it. `status` values must match the ones
   in features.njk and _data/extensions.json. If they drift, the
   two pages start contradicting each other.

   TWO RULES for this page:

   1. EVERY CARD IS A DELTA. If Mastodon ships it too, it is not a
      card. Demote it to the section's `parity` line. A card that
      describes something Mastodon already does is what gets the
      whole page dismissed by the one reader who knows Mastodon
      best. Check against *current* Mastodon before adding one.
   2. #gaps IS NOT OPTIONAL and is not padding. It is the reason
      this page can be linked in a fediverse thread. Never let a
      line in it become aspirational.

   Claim provenance: cards trace to bonfire-app: docs/CHANGELOG.md
   for anything with a status, docs/user_guides/ for anything a user
   does, docs/topics/federation-interoperability.md for the wire,
   masto_api_coverage.json for the API. Where the changelog and a
   user guide disagree, the changelog wins.

   Mastodon side last checked: August 2026 (joinmastodon.org, the
   public roadmap, and mastodon/mastodon CHANGELOG.md).

   Worked examples of the delta rule, so it doesn't get re-broken:
   · SSO: Mastodon IS an OAuth 2.0 authorization server ("Sign in
     with Mastodon" works; /oauth/authorize, /oauth/token,
     verify_credentials as pseudo-userinfo, and since 4.3 a
     /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server). It is NOT an OIDC
     provider: no id_token, no /.well-known/openid-configuration,
     no `openid` scope, open since mastodon#4800 (2017) and
     mastodon#26398 (2023). And it HAS been an OIDC client since
     mastodon#16221. So "SSO provider" is parity; only OIDC
     specifically is the delta. That's why the card says so.
   · Archipelago: Mastodon has had LIMITED_FEDERATION_MODE for
     years, so allow-list federation is not the delta. Granularity
     (naming people, not just servers) and governance (moderators
     in the UI, not an env var) are.
   ⚠️ RE-CHECK AT EACH MASTODON MINOR RELEASE. Several cards are one
   release away from becoming parity lines.
   ============================================================ #}

