<div class="relative overflow-x-clip bg-night text-ink font-body leading-[1.58] antialiased selection:bg-ember selection:text-[#160c02]">
  <div class="v2-ambient" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="relative z-[1]">

    {# ---------- hero ---------- #}
    <header class="pt-10 pb-[clamp(40px,5vw,60px)]" style="--acc:var(--color-flame)">
    <div class="max-w-[1140px] mx-auto px-7">
      <p class="mb-[26px] font-smono text-[.7rem] tracking-[.08em] text-ink-3"><a class="hover:text-spark" href="/">Bonfire</a><span class="mx-2">/</span>Mastodon vs Bonfire</p>
      <p class="{{ eyebrow }}"><i class="w-[9px] h-[9px] flex-none bg-[var(--acc)] [clip-path:polygon(50%_0,100%_50%,50%_100%,0_50%)]" aria-hidden="true"></i>Mastodon vs Bonfire</p>
      <h1 class="mt-[22px] font-disp font-semibold text-[clamp(2.1rem,5vw,3.7rem)] leading-[1.05] tracking-[-.02em] text-balance max-w-[22ch] [font-variation-settings:'opsz'_96]">You keep the network. Your community <span class="fire-text">gets a place in it.</span></h1>

      <p class="mt-[36px] text-[1.08rem] text-ink-2 max-w-[58ch] [&_b]:text-ink [&_b]:font-semibold">Already on Mastodon and wondering what Bonfire would actually give you? Not a different network. Bonfire speaks ActivityPub, so you follow and are followed by Mastodon accounts, your polls are votable from Mastodon, and many of the apps you already use work against its <b>Mastodon-compatible API</b>. <b>Nobody gets left behind.</b></p>

      <p class="mt-5 text-[1.08rem] text-ink-2 max-w-[58ch] [&_b]:text-ink [&_b]:font-semibold">Nobody has ever asked us for a better microblog. They ask for somewhere a community can live: with membership, a calendar, rules it wrote itself, a way to decide things together. That's the difference.</p>

      <p class="mt-5 text-[.95rem] text-ink-3 max-w-[58ch]">The two projects build in the open, and often together: Mastodon wrote the FEP for consent-based quoting and Bonfire shipped it alongside them, Bonfire added RFC 9421 message signatures with the wider ActivityPub community, and federated groups are being worked out at the W3C task force rather than as anyone's private dialect.</p>

      <nav class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-9" aria-label="Jump to a section">
        {%- for s in sections %}
        <a class="{{ jump }}" href="#{{ s.id }}">{{ s.eyebrow }}</a>
        {%- endfor %}
        <a class="{{ jump }}" href="#gaps">What Bonfire doesn't do</a>
      </nav>
    </div></header>

    <main>

    {# ---------- the delta ---------- #}
    {% for s in sections %}
    <section id="{{ s.id }}" class="py-[clamp(56px,7vw,96px)] border-t border-ink/[0.07] scroll-mt-[70px]" style="--acc:{{ s.acc }}">
    <div class="max-w-[1140px] mx-auto px-7">

      <p class="{{ eyebrow }}"><i class="w-[9px] h-[9px] flex-none bg-[var(--acc)] [clip-path:polygon(50%_0,100%_50%,50%_100%,0_50%)]" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{ s.eyebrow }}</p>
      <h2 class="{{ display }}">{{ s.head }} <span class="{{ 'corn-text' if s.acc == 'var(--color-corn)' else 'fire-text' }}">{{ s.headhl }}</span></h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-[1.02rem] text-ink-2 max-w-[44rem]">{{ s.intro | safe }}</p>

      {% if s.link %}<a class="{{ more }}" href="{{ s.link }}">{{ s.linktext }}</a>{% endif %}

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 min-[681px]:grid-cols-2 min-[1001px]:grid-cols-3 gap-3.5 mt-[34px]">
        {%- for c in s.cards %}
        <div class="{{ cell }}">
          <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
            <span class="{{ ic }}" aria-hidden="true"><i class="ph-duotone {{ c.icon }}"></i></span>
            {% if c.status %}<span class="{{ soon }}">{{ c.status }}</span>{% endif %}
          </div>
          <h3 class="{{ cellh }}">{{ c.name }}</h3>
          <p class="{{ cellp }}">{{ c.text | safe }}</p>
          {% if c.link %}<div class="mt-3">
            <a class="{{ cardlink }}" href="{{ c.link }}"{% if '//' in c.link %} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"{% endif %}>{{ c.linktext or 'Learn more' }} <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </div>{% endif %}
        </div>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>

      {# Parity, explicitly labelled. Anything Mastodon also ships belongs
         HERE and not in a card above. See the rules at the top of the file. #}
      {% if s.parity %}
      <p class="{{ paritybox }}">
        <span class="{{ paritylabel }}">Same as Mastodon</span>
        <span class="flex-1 min-w-[16rem] text-[.94rem] text-ink-2">{{ s.parity | safe }}</span>
      </p>
      {% endif %}

      {% if s.shot and s.img %}
      <figure class="m-0 mt-8">
        <img class="block mx-auto max-w-full max-h-[500px] w-auto rounded-xl border border-ink/15" src="/img/{{ s.img }}" alt="{{ s.shot }}" loading="lazy">
      </figure>
      {% endif %}

    </div></section>
    {% endfor %}

    {# ---------- the reverse ---------- #}
    <section id="gaps" class="py-[clamp(56px,7vw,96px)] border-t border-ink/[0.07] scroll-mt-[70px]" style="--acc:var(--color-corn)">
    <div class="max-w-[1140px] mx-auto px-7">

      <p class="{{ eyebrow }}"><i class="w-[9px] h-[9px] flex-none bg-[var(--acc)] [clip-path:polygon(50%_0,100%_50%,50%_100%,0_50%)]" aria-hidden="true"></i>The other direction</p>
      <h2 class="{{ display }}">What Bonfire <span class="corn-text">doesn't do.</span></h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-[1.02rem] text-ink-2 max-w-[44rem]">Mastodon has a decade of work behind it, and we federate with it rather than against it. Some of the below is what it does and we don't. Some are on our to-do list, others are deliberate trade-offs.</p>

      <div class="{{ flatcell }} mt-[34px]">
        <ul class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          {%- for g in gaps %}
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 {{ '' if loop.first else 'pt-4 border-t border-ink/[0.07]' }}">
            <span class="mt-[9px] w-[7px] h-[7px] flex-none bg-ink-3/50 [clip-path:polygon(50%_0,100%_50%,50%_100%,0_50%)]" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="{{ cellp }} [&_b]:text-ink [&_b]:font-semibold">{{ g.text | safe }}{% if g.byChoice %} <span class="{{ soon }} !text-leaf !border-leaf/30 ml-1 align-[.15em]">By choice</span>{% endif %}</span>
          </li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-6 font-smono text-[.68rem] text-ink-3 max-w-[62ch] leading-[1.7]">Both sides of this page are checked against Mastodon's changelog and roadmap, and against Bonfire's own. Last checked August 2026. Spotted something wrong or out of date? <a class="text-spark hover:underline" href="/contact">Tell us and we'll fix it.</a></p>

    </div></section>

    {# ---------- coming from mastodon ---------- #}
    <section class="py-[clamp(56px,7vw,90px)] border-t border-ink/[0.07]" style="--acc:var(--color-leaf)">
    <div class="max-w-[1140px] mx-auto px-7">
      <p class="{{ eyebrow }}"><i class="w-[9px] h-[9px] flex-none bg-[var(--acc)] [clip-path:polygon(50%_0,100%_50%,50%_100%,0_50%)]" aria-hidden="true"></i>Coming from Mastodon</p>
      <h2 class="{{ display }}">You can bring <span class="fire-text">all of it with you.</span></h2>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-8 gap-y-3 mt-8">
        <a class="{{ more }} !mt-0" href="/features#data">Import your account, follows and posts <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a class="{{ more }} !mt-0" href="https://campground.bonfire.cafe" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wander the demo first <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a class="{{ more }} !mt-0" href="/start">Install an instance <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a class="{{ more }} !mt-0" href="/compare">How Bonfire compares to non-fediverse tools <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    {# ---------- closing CTA ---------- #}
    <section class="text-center pt-[clamp(60px,8vw,110px)] pb-[clamp(80px,9vw,140px)] border-t border-ink/[0.07]">
    <div class="max-w-[1140px] mx-auto px-7">
      <h2 class="mx-auto font-disp font-[560] text-[clamp(2rem,4.6vw,3.4rem)] leading-[1.05] text-balance [font-variation-settings:'opsz'_96]">Same fediverse. <span class="italic font-medium text-flame">A world of your own.</span></h2>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3.5 mt-[34px]">
        <a class="{{ btnfire }}" href="/start">Get started</a>
        <a class="{{ btnline }}" href="https://campground.bonfire.cafe" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wander the demo</a>
        <a class="{{ btnline }}" href="/compare">The wider comparison</a>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-[26px] font-smono text-[.82rem] text-ink-3">Missing a block? <a class="text-spark border-b border-spark/35 pb-0.5 hover:border-spark" href="/contact">Tell us what your community needs.</a></p>
    </div></section>

    </main>
  </div>
</div>